#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/index.md:30
msgid "The one habit that matters more than the rest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/index.md:32
msgid ""
"**Every rule you write down says how many pages it was measured on, and "
"the number travels with it.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/index.md:35
msgid ""
"This is not a style preference. A format is a claim about a layout, and a"
" layout is only knowable by looking: an anchor read off the page in front"
" of you is a hypothesis, and the difference between a hypothesis and a "
"rule is a count. The project has paid for the difference more than once, "
"and the cheapest of those lessons is on the next page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/index.md:40
msgid ""
"The commands that produce the count are two, and neither of them is the "
"test suite:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/index.md:47
msgid ""
"The first says where a text occurs before any format exists; the second "
"says how the format classifies every page of the document once one does. "
"Between them they turn *\"it works on page 25\"* into *\"it holds on 983 "
"pages of 1 261, and the 80 it leaves out are these\"*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/index.md:51
msgid "What this area assumes you have read"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/index.md:53
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{doc}`../selections`, because almost everything written in these steps is"
" a selection, and {doc}`../dev-loop`, because every measurement here is "
"one of its four commands. The levels themselves — what a row, a YAML "
"block and a Python module can each say — are {doc}`../advanced/index`."
msgstr ""

